evidence = "hf-build and hf-done record the exact same candidate revision, command, exit code and private log in /out/run/gates.jsonl; the final response copies the last hf-done evidence line. The record does not invent a successful revision before the gates execute."
implementation = "Replace the incomplete explicit chain with recursive source-based test discovery, a complete manifest classification of Anvil/private suites, separately documented probe commands and a CI command that includes every non-private suite. Validate source entries and compiled artifacts before execution; run each suite in its own real Node process, continue through failures, and propagate any launch error, signal or nonzero exit. No existing test or assertion is changed."
source_proof = "Pytest parses package.json and tsconfig.json, inventories all maintained test sources, checks all previous entries remain runnable, asserts previously omitted interface/proof/recovery suites enter the default command, and checks recursive discovery, source-to-compiled mapping, subprocess invocation, failure propagation, guarded probe inputs, documentation and finding-to-test mapping against the actual files."
review_only = "The JavaScript runner, TypeScript compiler, TypeScript assertions, live node, Anvil, cross-language programs, private case harness and CI workflow jobs are not executed by this Python-only source qualification. Existing recovery suites are inventoried and their registered production-path tests checked, not run here. CI execution requires the separately owned wiring below; this task does not claim a green npm test, a live restart proof or deployed CI coverage."

